I think the biggest thing that I'm  learning in this moment with launching  my own brand is that being able to  approach it very curiously is a very  important way to be as an entrepreneur  this is a huge learning process for me  and I'm literally learning as I go  [Music]  I've just always had such an obsession  with skin care and growing up my mom and  my grandma always had an obsession with  skin care and beauty and I feel like  they really Infuse That Into Me growing  up so as I got older and when I started  modeling and working in that industry I  felt like I really started to learn a  lot more about skin care and Beauty  through working with different makeup  artists and estheticians and facialists  and so many people who are experts in  their field and I feel like it really  helped me develop what My Philosophy is  on beauty and that is what really drove  me to want to start my own brand  [Music]  I think it's something that I always had  a dream of doing I just didn't really  know how to do that or where to start  and then  when the pandemic hit I felt like I had  finally  really known how I would approach  starting a beauty brand and I knew that  I wanted that to be in skin care first  and I felt like in that moment I had the  time to really pursue it and that's  where it started for me  I think my favorite part of this whole  entire process is  the creative process and that I get to  be in charge of the creative process a  lot of the time you know I've lent my  name and my face to other people's  creative process and I think that  actually has helped me develop mine in a  lot of ways but it feels very empowering  to to be the one that is in charge and I  think the thing that has prepared me  from being in the industry before is  honestly on the creative side of things  I've had the privilege of working with  so many different creatives and I think  that each time I've worked with somebody  new I've absorbed you know their energy  and I've gotten to see the way that they  work and I think that if you allow  yourself to be a sponge then you absorb  that information and you can pour it  into your own creative process  the most surprising part about this for  me so far has honestly been the response  that I've seen since launching the brand  the last two restocks we've had of our  peptide glazing fluid sold 24 units per  second and we've had a wait list of over  600 000 people  I think that when you are  launching a brand baby you have so many  hopes for it and you know you have a lot  of dreams for what the response might be  but you don't really know until it's out  there in the world and people get their  hands on your product and give honest  feedback and I've been very very  overwhelmed in the in the most positive  way by the feedback and I feel really  really grateful for that  when we were creating our goals and  putting together kind of the Pyramid of  what is the most important thing for me  when creating this these products it's  been you know effective efficacious  great packaging really having people  feel like they are having an experience  with the products it's really resonating  with people and that was my biggest goal  with the brand that when they got their  hands on the products they would really  actually love the packaging that they  would actually love the physical product  inside that it would be effective and  really be just a great product all  around I think social media is a huge  resource and it's huge for building a  brand in this moment in time and the  response from from everything from Tick  Tock from Instagram has been really  really positive which I'm really really  happy about and just the beauty  community in general especially on Tick  Tock and especially on Instagram the  fact that they have embraced it the way  that they have is just really special to  me and I could not be doing this without  the people who  have spoken about the products and  really love them  foreign  it's never going to go perfectly and  there's always going to be bumps along  the way there's always going to be  mishaps and I think my goal is to  continuously be a curious person in the  space because it only helps your brand  get better and better when you learn  from the mistakes and move forward  [Music]
 

